# HTTP(S) REST Communication Rules (Tc3_IotBase)

Libraries: `Tc3_IotBase`, `Tc3_JsonXml`. Core FBs: `FB_IotHttpClient`, `FB_IotHttpRequest`, `FB_IotHttpHeaderFieldMap`.

## Mandatory Rules

1. **Internal state** — Every HTTP client FB: `_bBusy`, `_bConnected`, `_bError`, `_sError`, `_fbClient`, `_fbRequest`, `_fbHeader`, `_fbTonTimeout`, `_sPath` (`instance-path` / `noinit`).
2. **Execute every cycle** — After init, `_fbClient.Execute()` every cycle. One TON on `_bBusy` for timeout recovery (MEMSET busy flags on timeout).
3. **Send = 2-state CASE** — State 0 Build & Send; State 1 Evaluate with flat ELSIF. `VAR_INST` for `_nState`. Return `TRUE` only when fully processed in State 1.
4. **Reset once** — `_bBusy` / `_nState` reset at end of State 1 only.
5. **JSON DOM** — Always validate `_jsonDoc <> 0` after `GetJsonDomContent`.
6. **JSON payload lifetime** — `__DELETE(_pJsonPayload)` in State 0 after `SendRequest` (not State 1). `nContentSize := size - 1` (exclude null terminator).
7. **3-level error eval** (flat ELSIF):

| Level | Condition | `_bConnected` | `_bError` |
|-------|-----------|---------------|-----------|
| 1 | `_fbClient.bError` | `FALSE` | `TRUE` |
| 2 | `_fbRequest.bError` | `FALSE` | `TRUE` |
| 3 | status outside 200–207 | `TRUE` | `TRUE` |
| OK | status 200–207 | `TRUE` | `FALSE` |

8. **Error mapping** — Every HTTP library needs `F_[Lib]_HttpRequestErrorToString`.
9. **Auth headers** — `AddField(..., bAppendValue := FALSE)`.
10. **Properties** — Expose `IsConnected`, `IsBusy`, `IsError`, `ErrorText`.

## Checklist (new HTTP library)

- [ ] `FB_[Lib]_Client` with mandatory state
- [ ] `Execute` (init, cycle, timeout, outputs)
- [ ] `F_[Lib]_HttpRequestErrorToString`
- [ ] `ST_[Lib]_HttpParam` (host, port, token, TLS, timeout)
- [ ] Each Send: 2-state CASE, flat ELSIF, 3-level errors
- [ ] `_jsonDoc <> 0` after every `GetJsonDomContent`
- [ ] `__DELETE` payload in State 0 after send

